# Auto commit & push

After finishing a set of code/doc changes in this repo, **commit and push to the current branch without waiting to be asked**.

Follow the existing git safety protocol:

- Never update git config
- Never force-push to main/master
- Never use `--amend` unless the usual amend conditions are met
- Never skip hooks
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens)
- Prefer excluding unrelated untracked folders (e.g. `google-ads-assets/` unless the user asked for them)
- Use a concise commit message focused on why
- Push with `git push` (set upstream if needed)

If there is nothing to commit, skip. If push fails, report the error and stop.
